<title>USA: MAIC Holdings Inc Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>MAIC Holdings Inc Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, Ala. 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>						     Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							     March 31,</p>
<p>							    1997	 1996</p>
<p> Total revenues				     $38,471   $30,260</p>
<p>Income before income taxes and minority</p>
<p>  interests					    11,093     8,494</p>
<p> NET INCOME					     8,414     6,856</p>
<p>Earnings per share:</p>
<p> Net income						 .82	 .69</p>
<p> Operating earnings				     .81	 .69</p>
<p>Weighted average number of common shares</p>
<p>    outstanding during the year		  10,274     9,931</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said it acquired MOMED Holding Co, the parent company of Missouri Medical Insurance Co in December 1996 and Q1 1997 results are consolidated.</p>
<p>The 330,000 shares issued as part of the MOMED transaction affect only 1997 results, it said.</p>
<p>The company said Q1 1997 revenues increased as result of continuing expansion, including its acquisition MOMED.</p>
<p>Q1 1997 earnings per share are calculated as if the additional 581,000 shares issued as a result of the December 1996 stock dividend were outstanding throughout 1996, it said.</p>
